{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385443-entropy-encouraging-positivity","id":1385443,"title":"Entropy + Encouraging Positivity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-03T12:19:19-07:00","id":1385443,"title":"Entropy + Encouraging Positivity","content":"Greetings.<br /> <br /> I play a psychic medium Lightworker who is trying to appeal to her patron spirits and the universe to quell the frequency of fights, riots, and death in her town. When I first thought of a way to do this sphere-wise, Entropy immediately came to mind (after all, shifting probability towards a peaceful disposition seems to fit the sphere's abilities.) But M20's How Do You Do That mentions that entropy effects can only address actions/events that are happening, not what might happen or what could happen.<br /> <br /> My question is, with that in mind what sphere would I use to bind aggression/conflict/fighting in a certain area that is not correspondence? (I know wards can do something of the sort, but I suspect other spheres like entropy can do it, too)<br /> <br /> To illustrate this example better: Imagine her calling upon an angel or the universal force of positivity and serenity to soak a certain area, and thus make it difficult to do actions to the contrary of those principles.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T13:12:37-07:00","id":1385451,"title":"","content":"First, it would be hard to get away from Correspondence when trying to make your effect city wide. From there though Mind 2 can be used to difuse emotions which would certainly be where the root of the problems of disharmony would be. <br /> <br /> Entropy most certainly can be used but you would need it to Rank 5 in order to give birth to harmonious thoughts that could then take hold in the populous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T11:48:51-07:00","id":1385630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385443-entropy-encouraging-positivity?p=1385451#post1385451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, it would be hard to get away from Correspondence when trying to make your effect city wide. From there though Mind 2 can be used to difuse emotions which would certainly be where the root of the problems of disharmony would be.<br /> <br /> Entropy most certainly can be used but you would need it to Rank 5 in order to give birth to harmonious thoughts that could then take hold in the populous.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But what if the people doing the violence are immune to mental effects? Would the correspondence ward become useless?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T12:16:16-07:00","id":1385634,"title":"","content":"I wasn't thinking establishing a ward, my point was you'd need Correspondence more for range and effecting areas beyond you sight. You're more interested in establishing a continual emotion altering effect that lingers with a duration. It will most assuredly require a ritual with quite a few successes in order to have a city wide effect. At least 15, maybe more successes.<br /> <br /> As far as having people immune to the effect i would say you would have to deal with supernaturals in the target area in person. Your effect will pretty much be limited to sleepers and supernaturals of low Willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T17:51:42-07:00","id":1385695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385443-entropy-encouraging-positivity?p=1385634#post1385634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't thinking establishing a ward, my point was you'd need Correspondence more for range and effecting areas beyond you sight. You're more interested in establishing a continual emotion altering effect that lingers with a duration. It will most assuredly require a ritual with quite a few successes in order to have a city wide effect. At least 15, maybe more successes.<br /> <br /> As far as having people immune to the effect i would say you would have to deal with supernaturals in the target area in person. Your effect will pretty much be limited to sleepers and supernaturals of low Willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is a &quot;smart ward&quot; that wards against violence or a particular devilish action in the city a feasible alternative to the mind effect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T18:27:07-07:00","id":1385700,"title":"","content":"The only way to ward against an attitude, emotion, or thought would be with Mind. Which would need Correspondence 4 and Mind 2 at a minimum. It will also require quite a bit of Quintessence. <br /> <br /> Also, though I'm no expert on Wards due to my group never really using them, I'm pretty sure it would keep out the people of the mindset you target. Which really just leaves a bunch of hostile people getting even more angry sitting outside the warded area.<br /> <br /> One idea I came up with thinking about this today was turning 1 or more people into sort of a Living Charm that would create a propetuating effect that spread from individual to individual. This of course would require Mind 2+ along with Prime 3(I think for living g charms) some quintessence, and possibly Entropy 3 to be contingent upon who it spreads too. No since spreading it to people already effected. Just a thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}